{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-101258",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=20,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{15}{20}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{3}{4}\\,{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=20,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
